To optimize your Nginx configuration for load balancing and handle more requests per second while maintaining high uptime, you can make several improvements. Here are some suggestions:

### 1. Add More Backend Servers
If you have multiple backend servers, you can distribute the load more effectively. Ensure that all backend servers are capable of handling the load.

### 2. Use Proper Load Balancing Algorithms
Choose the appropriate load balancing algorithm based on your needs. Common algorithms include `round-robin`, `least-connected`, and `ip_hash`.

### 3. Enable Connection Pooling
Enable connection pooling to reuse connections and reduce overhead.

### 4. Increase Worker Connections
Increase the number of worker connections to handle more concurrent connections.

### 5. Enable Keepalive Connections
Enable keepalive connections to reduce the overhead of establishing new connections.

### 6. Use Proper Buffer Sizes
